syntax tests: name bash 5.3 when skipping for its absence

The external shell tests require bash 5.3 through onceHasBash53, but the
message they skip or fail with still asked for bash 5.2, which sends
someone with bash 5.2 installed looking for the wrong problem.

Reproducer, before this change, with bash 5.2 on PATH:

	$ REQUIRE_SHELLS=1 go test -run TestParseConfirm ./syntax

fails with "bash 5.2 required to run".

diff --git a/syntax/parser_test.go b/syntax/parser_test.go
index ba298b6..2d153b1 100644
--- a/syntax/parser_test.go
+++ b/syntax/parser_test.go
@@ -264,7 +264,7 @@ func skipExternal(tb testing.TB, message string) {
 var externalShells = map[LangVariant]externalShell{
 	LangBash: {"bash", func(tb testing.TB) {
 		if !onceHasBash53() {
-			skipExternal(tb, "bash 5.2 required to run")
+			skipExternal(tb, "bash 5.3 required to run")
 		}
 	}},
 	LangPOSIX: {"dash", func(tb testing.TB) {
